.TH PKCSEP11_MIGRATE 1 "August 2026" "@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "openCryptoki"
.SH NAME
pkcsep11_migrate \- utility to re-encrypt EP11 token keys to prepare a
change of master keys in the EP11 adapter

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpkcsep11_migrate\fP
[\fB-h\fP | \fB--help\fP]
\fB-slot\fP \fIslot-number\fP \fB-adapter\fP \fIadapter-ID\fP
\fB-domain\fP \fIdomain-ID\fP

.SH DESCRIPTION
In case of a master key change within an EP11 adapter, all key objects that are
wrapped with this master key must be re-wrapped or re-encrypted.
The \fBpkcsep11_migrate\fP utility takes all EP11 token-related key objects
that are wrapped with the EP11 adapter master key, decrypts each key object
with the current master key, and encrypts it with the new master key.

Notes:
.br
1. The new master key must be set and committed on the EP11 adapter via the
Trusted Key Entry (TKE) console before using this utility.
.br
2. While this tool is running, no process using the EP11 token should be running.
.br
3. Before using this tool, make a backup of the token objects in
   \fBep11tok/TOK_OBJ/\fP.
.br
4. After successful execution of the migrate utility and before (re)starting
   programs using the EP11 token, the new master key must be activated using
   the TKE.
.br
5. The utility prompts for the USER PIN of the EP11 token.

.SH "COMMAND SUMMARY"
.IP "\fB-slot\fP \fIslot-number\fP" 10
Specifies the token slot of the EP11 token. This option is required. The slot
number must be specified in decimal notation.
.IP "\fB-adapter\fP \fIadapter-ID\fP" 10
Specifies an EP11 adapter ID. This option is required.
(Refer to \fBlszcrypt\fP to get a list of installed crypto adapters.)
The adapter ID can be specified in hexadecimal (for example, \fB0x0A\fP) or
in decimal notation.
.IP "\fB-domain\fP \fIdomain-ID\fP" 10
Specifies the usage domain for the EP11 adapter. This option is required.
(Refer to \fBlszcrypt\fP to get a list of installed crypto domains.)
The domain ID can be specified in hexadecimal (for example, \fB0x0B\fP) or in
decimal notation.
.IP "\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP" 10
Show usage information.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP "\fBPKCSLIB\fP" 10
Specifies the PKCS#11 library to load. If not set, \fBlibopencryptoki.so\fP
is used.
.IP "\fBOCK_EP11_LIBRARY\fP" 10
Specifies the EP11 host library to load. If not set, the utility tries
\fBlibep11.so.4\fP, \fBlibep11.so.3\fP, \fBlibep11.so.2\fP,
\fBlibep11.so.1\fP, and \fBlibep11.so\fP.

.SH SEE ALSO
.PD 0
.TP
\fBpkcsconf\fP(1),
.TP
\fBopencryptoki\fP(7),
.TP
\fBpkcsslotd\fP(8).
.PD
